# Astro Page Conventions

Every page wraps content in the shared layout and follows this pattern:

```astro
---
import Layout from '../layouts/Default.astro';
---

<Layout title="Page Name" section="section-id">
  <h1 class="page-title">Page Name</h1>
  <p class="page-sub">Short description · separated · by middots</p>

  <!-- page content -->

  <div class="footer">Nexus Design System · Page Name</div>
</Layout>
```

## Rules
- `title` — shown in `<title>` tag, appended with " — Nexus Design System"
- `section` — must match the `id` in the nav items array in `Default.astro` for active state highlighting
- Title is always `<h1 class="page-title">`, subtitle is always `<p class="page-sub">`
- When adding a new page, also add a nav entry in `src/layouts/Default.astro`
- Subdirectories (atoms/, molecules/, organisms/) use `index.astro` for the landing page
- Use British English for the filename (e.g. `colours.astro`, not `colors.astro`)
